LOG of the CHANGES in the package ICtest

Version 0.3-8:

* New functions FOBIaug and SIRaug for the augmentation estimators of FOBI and SIR

* New function PCAaugHD for the high-dimensional augmentation estimator of Radojicic and Virta (2025)

* ladleplot and ggladleplot respect the new optional element index.start of ladle objects

* PCAschott now implements the high-dimensional test of Schott (2006), which it was documented to be, and can be used also for p > n. The likelihood
  ratio test it computed before is available as the new function PCAlrt. Results of PCAschott therefore differ from earlier versions.

* Bug fixes:
  - PCAlrt (formerly PCAschott): Lawley's correction factor fixed (this also fixes the infinite statistic for k = 0) and the returned components S are now Xc W
  - NGPP, NGPPsim, NGPPest: the "tanh" and "gauss" objectives and their gradients now subtract the expectations under normality
  - NGPP, NGPPsim, NGPPest: invalid non-linearities, an unknown method or a wrong length of alpha now give an error
  - NGPPsim, NGPPest: data.name is now the name of the data
  - kSearch: backward search returns the smallest k when no test rejects, and the test is recognized also when called as ICtest::PCAasymp etc.
  - FOBIboot, ICSboot: strategy B1 returns S with column names
  - PCAboot: strategy B2 standardized the principal components with 1/D instead of 1/sqrt(D), so the bootstrap samples did not have the
    radial distribution of the data and the test did not keep its level (conservative for normal data). The help page now also states that B2 assumes elliptical data
  - all tests check k; PCAasymp, PCAschott, PCAboot and ICSboot allow 0 <= k <= p-2, the others 0 <= k <= p-1
  - PCAladle, FOBIladle, SIRladle, PCAaug, SIRboot accept data frames; the ladle functions check ncomp
  - covSIR handles a discrete response or a factor and ties; SIRasymp uses the number of slices actually used for the degrees of freedom
  - p-values computed with lower.tail = FALSE for better precision

* Added regression tests in tests/regression.R

* Typos in the method names of PCAasymp and FOBIasymp fixed ("subsphericity", "subgaussianity"), kSearch prints a final newline only after
  a progress bar, and the PCA vignette describes the corrected strategy B2 of PCAboot

* Help page of rorth rewritten: it now describes the sign correction of the QR decomposition, cites Mezzadri (2007) and
  has an example comparing rorth with the uncorrected QR decomposition

* Changes after a code review:
  - FOBIboot, ICSboot, SIRboot: p-values now use #(T* >= T), as PCAboot and the documentation, instead of #(T* > T)
  - NGPPsim, NGPPest: p-values are now (#(T* >= T) + 1)/(N + 1) and can no longer be zero, results therefore differ
    slightly from earlier versions
  - NGPP checks that 1 <= k <= p, NGPPsim that 0 <= k <= p - 1, and the weights alpha must lie in [0, 1]
  - naug, nrep, n.boot and N must be positive integers in all augmentation, bootstrap and NGPP functions
  - plot, ggplot and components give an informative error for ladle objects without components (as returned by ladle)
  - kSearch: invalid or empty ranges of min_dim and max_dim give an error, an unsuccessful search returns k = NA,
    and the help page states the monotonicity assumption of the binary search
  - NGPP, NGPPsim, NGPPest: numerically stable computation of log(cosh(x)) for the "tanh" objective
  - help page fixes in NGPPsim (range of k, class htest, typo)

Version 0.3-7:

* Updating makevars files
* Removing components as a generic function as it is now a generic function in ICS which is imported

Version 0.3-6:

* Fixing some missing links in help files when linking to functions in external packages
* Fixing a bug in rorth
* Adding K. Perkonoja as package author
* New function kSearch including print and summary methods


Version 0.3-5:
* Added function ICSboot
* Added function PCAaug
* Fixed some bug in bootstrapping functions when k=0


Version 0.3-4:
* Added a new generic function ggscreeplot and made the earlier ggscreeplot its method for the class ictest

Version 0.3-3:
* fixed NGPP so that it also allows extracting only a single direction, k = 1
* updated some documentation
* added fICA to suggests
* changed the maintainer email

Version 0.3-2:
* plot.ictest, plot.ladle, ggplot.ictest and ggplot.ladle can now also handle sources which are of class zoo and xts
* adding the ggplot.ladle function

Version 0.3-1:
* modfiying some plotting functions to use time series plots if S is a multivariate time series

Version 0.3:
* several bug fixes
* improving documentation
* new function PCAschott
* adding the ladle methdology together with methods


Version 0.2:

First version released on CRAN
